WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.860
Connect a red LED to a variable
supply, and slowly turn up the voltage.

2
00:00:05.910 --> 00:00:06.890
Nothing.

3
00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:08.150
Still nothing.

4
00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:12.410
Then, at 1.96 volts, it starts to glow.

5
00:00:12.460 --> 00:00:17.580
Swap in a blue or a green LED, and it
switches on at a different voltage.

6
00:00:17.630 --> 00:00:22.480
Why should the voltage that switches on
an LED depend on the light it gives out?

7
00:00:22.530 --> 00:00:26.630
In this mission, you'll measure the
threshold voltage of several LEDs,

8
00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:28.370
using a simple circuit.

9
00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:33.020
Then you'll plot your results, and use
the graph to measure the Planck constant.

10
00:00:33.070 --> 00:00:38.160
Your mission: explain why an LED's switch-on
voltage depends on the light it gives

11
00:00:38.210 --> 00:00:38.690
out.
